      "message": "The logic that checks the command type is hard to follow.  Can you redo these checks to query the `init_local_state` instead?\n\nMaybe setup the init states like:\n```\n\t/** Enable the PDC */\n\tINIT_PDC_ENABLE,\n\t/** Get the PDC IC Status */\n\tINIT_PDC_GET_IC_STATUS,\n\t/** Set the PDC Notifications */\n\tINIT_PDC_SET_NOTIFICATION_ENABLE,\n\t/** Reset the PDC */\n\tINIT_PDC_RESET,\n\t/** Initialization done */\n\tINIT_PDC_COMPLETE\n```\nThen when you\u0027re going to set the state, you can just do \n```\nif (data-\u003einit_local_state !\u003d INIT_PDC_COMPLETE)\n    set_state(ST_INIT);\nelse\n    set_state(ST_IDLE);\n```\n\n\n\nAlso, it\u0027s not clear why you are going back to `ST_INIT:INIT_PDC_ENABLE` after the reset completes.  The comment at line 457 indicates you should be transitioning to`ST_IDLE`.",
